{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NetworkLib"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Using Completion Handlers"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingCallbacks","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Connect and send data using the callback-based socket API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingProxies","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/TypedMessages","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/HTTPHeaders"],"title":"API usage examples","generated":true,"anchor":"API-usage-examples"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocket","type":"reference"},{"text":" provides completion handlers alongside its asynchronous methods. This example sends a payload to a local TCP service and closes the connection once the send completes.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Send to a local service","type":"heading","anchor":"Send-to-a-local-service","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Run a TCP service listening on port 9000 before calling this function. The service must accept the example’s UTF-8 payload.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import Network","import NetworkLib","","func sendWithCallbacks(","    completion: @escaping @Sendable (Result<Void, NWError>) -> Void",") throws -> RawSocket {","    let configuration = RawSocketConfiguration(","        \"127.0.0.1\",","        9000,","        isSecure: false,","        timeout: 10","    )","    let socket = try RawSocket(configuration)","","    socket.connect { result in","        switch result {","        case .success:","            socket.send(Data(\"hello\\n\".utf8)) { sendResult in","                socket.cancel {","                    completion(sendResult)","                }","            }","        case .failure(let error):","            socket.cancel {","                completion(.failure(error))","            }","        }","    }","    return socket","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Retain the returned socket while the operation is in progress. You can call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"socket.cancel(nil)"},{"text":" to stop it early. A successful send means that the connection processed the bytes; it doesn’t confirm that the server processed the application message.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choose a callback queue","anchor":"Choose-a-callback-queue","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The initializer accepts a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"delegateQueue"},{"text":" argument. Without it, callbacks run on NetworkLib’s shared socket delegate queue. Completion handlers are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"text":"; synchronize any shared mutable state and use an explicit actor hop before updating actor-isolated UI state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The example disables TLS for its local plaintext service. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isSecure: true"},{"text":" when connecting to a TLS-enabled server.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Run the CLI example","anchor":"Run-the-CLI-example","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From a local checkout of NetworkLib, run this command in the directory containing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["swift run Examples callbacks"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before running, start a TCP listener in another terminal with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nc -l 9000"},{"text":". The listener displays the payload; the CLI reports when the send has been processed and the socket has closed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The runnable implementation is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/Examples\/CallbackExample.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"reference"},{"text":" for tool requirements, the complete command list, and shared CLI behavior.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/networklib\/usingcallbacks"]}],"references":{"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RunningExamples":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/runningexamples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run the documented API examples from the terminal using the repository’s Examples target."}],"title":"Running the Examples"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/HTTPHeaders":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/HTTPHeaders","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Working with HTTP Headers","abstract":[{"text":"Use typed header keys with Foundation requests.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/httpheaders"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/SendingAndReceiving":{"kind":"article","title":"Sending and Receiving Data","abstract":[{"text":"Connect securely, send bytes, and read a response with async\/await.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/sendingandreceiving","type":"topic"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RawSocket":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocket","abstract":[{"text":"A socket that sends and receives raw data or protocol-framed messages over a Network framework connection.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RawSocket","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RawSocket","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RawSocket","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/rawsocket"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/TypedMessages":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/TypedMessages","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Exchanging Typed UDP Messages","abstract":[{"text":"Represent a UTF-8 datagram with the socket’s message protocols.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/typedmessages"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib","kind":"symbol","title":"NetworkLib","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/networklib","abstract":[{"text":"Build socket connections with Swift concurrency and Apple’s Network framework.","type":"text"}]},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/UsingProxies":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingProxies","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Connecting Through an HTTP Proxy","abstract":[{"text":"Configure an HTTP CONNECT tunnel with optional authentication.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/usingproxies"}}}